or pins) connect to other nets. The VREF+_FCC filter net lands on pin 13 (PH1) instead of pin 20 (VREF+).\", \"expected\": \"The 25 MHz crystal (HSE1) should be on the STM32H7 oscillator pins PH0/PH1 (pins 12/13), and VREF+ should be on pin 20, as in the NAVC design where HSE sits on PH0/PH1.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"Page 2 (FCC): \\\"HSE_IN_FCC\\\" and \\\"HSE_OUT_FCC\\\" labels at the left edge of FCC1 next to pin 5 and pin 37; pin list \\\"PH0 12 PH1 13 ... PE6 5 PE7 37\\\"\"}, {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"\\\"HSE crystal (both MCUs) | FCC / NAVC | ABM8G-25.000MHZ-4Y-T3 | FCC.sch, NAVC.sch notes 'High Speed External Crystal'\\\"\"}], \"impact\": \"If the crystal is on non-oscillator pins the FCC cannot run from HSE and will fail to clock correctly; VREF+ on the wrong pin would degrade ADC reference accuracy.\", \"confidence\": 0.3}], \"summary\": \"The FCC sheet inserts an undocumented 74LVC1G34 buffer (U11) on the UART2 link to the NAVC, with a 'Troj_UART_IN' net name, which the spec does not describe and which is consistent with deliberate tampering. A secondary concern is that the FCC crystal and VREF+ nets appear on non-standard MCU pins.\"}",
